# .scaffold-once-skills — portable skill TEMPLATES that seed a consuming
# project's .claude/skills/<name>/ once, on the first sync where that
# directory is absent, then are never overwritten again. The consuming
# project owns the file from that point on.
#
# This is a third mode, distinct from both:
#   - a normal portable skill (always resynced from skills/<name>/)
#   - pipekit/.local-skills (a CONSUMING project's manifest; never touched
#     by sync at all, declared by the project, not by pipekit)
#
# Add a name here only when the skill's value is project-specific curation
# that a normal resync would destroy — see sop/Lane_Map_SOP.md for the
# worked example and sop/Skills_SOP.md § Syncing Portable Skills for the
# mechanism. Most skills should stay normally portable; this list should
# stay short.

lane-map
